<p class="lead">The Bear Species XT RTH is the bow many hunters end up with when they want a complete, forgiving setup without paying flagship prices. It pairs a compact 30-inch frame with a 6.75-inch brace height and a 320 fps speed rating, then ships with the sight, rest and quiver already in the box. If you have been searching for the Bear Species XT RTH compound bow and wondering whether it is enough bow for deer season, this review lays out the facts.</p>

<p>Below you will find verified Bear Species XT specs, a plain-English look at the single-cam draw cycle, what the RTH package actually includes, and a side-by-side comparison with the Bear Alaskan XT RTH. We also cover who should buy it, who should skip it, and what to add before your first hunt.</p>

<h2 id="h-bear-species-xt-specs">Bear Species XT RTH Specs</h2>
<p>These numbers are drawn from Lancaster Archery and other retailer listings that agree with each other. Where sources disagree, we say so rather than pick a number.</p>
